# the map region drawn in the outdoors ground: an ONS code from /boundaries'
# geojson, empty for the whole constituency. Yours, not the device's — which
# ward you are working is a fact about you, and it should follow you from the
# phone to the laptop the way /current-project's project does.
#
# No js: column on purpose. A bridged key is republished at /payload's older
# link, so a page reading it after a write made from this node — newer than
# /payload — would paint one frame of the previous region (misses.md,
# "navigation from the wrong side"). The page learns the code from the
# `#misoRegion` marker this node's own render writes instead.
region: String = String::new() (user, last-write, own)
